hed with full feature access and no usage-based limits through September 2026\"</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://clawtick.com\" target=\"_blank\">ClawTick</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source-badge\">Product Hunt</div>\n                    <div class=\"tag\">workflow agent</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        A cloud scheduler built specifically for AI agents. Schedule LangChain, CrewAI, or webhook tasks with one CLI command, featuring monitoring, alerts, and retries.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Released: 2026-05-09</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Cron jobs for AI agents w/ one command, zero infrastructure\"</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Schedule LangChain, CrewAI, or webhook tasks with one CLI command\"</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2>Whitelist Updates</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI 0.129.0 and Chrome Extension</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-version\">Version 0.129.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"source-badge\">release</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        New Codex CLI version 0.129.0 with modal Vim editing in composer, improved TUI workflows, theme-aware status line, plugin workspace sharing, and enhanced hooks. Also introduced Codex for Chrome extension for working with apps and websites in the browser.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Updated: 2026-05-07</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf 2.2.17 - Devin Review & Quick Review</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-version\">Version 2.2.17</div>\n                    <div class=\"source-badge\">feature</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        All Windsurf IDE users now have access to Devin Review and Quick Review with existing subscription. Added Agent Command Center improvements including list display option and improved sessions sidebar. Fixed bugs with MCP servers and improved Devin Local agent reliability.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Updated: 2026-05-06</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI v0.40.0 - Offline Search and Advanced Resource Management</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-version\">Version v0.40.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"source-badge\">release</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Bundled ripgrep for offline search support and added GitHub-style colorblind themes. Introduced MCP resource tools and transitioned to a prompt-driven, four-tier memory management system. Enabled topic update narrations by default and streamlined Gemma local model setup.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Updated: 2026-04-28</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xn-gtHDsaPY\" target=\"_blank\">7 Open Source AI Tools for Agent Development in 2026</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Fireship covers emerging open source tools reflecting shift toward 'vibe engineering'. Features: Agency Agents, PromptFoo (acquired by OpenAI), MicroFish, Impeccable, OpenViking, Heretic, and NanoChat.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xn-gtHDsaPY\" target=\"_blank\">Fireship</a> | YouTube\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">PromptFoo</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">vibe engineering</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-03-12</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/state-of-llms-2025\" target=\"_blank\">The State of LLMs 2025: From DeepSeek R1 to RLVR Dominance</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        2025 dominated by reasoning models using RLVR and GRPO. Training costs may be 10x cheaper than assumed. 'Benchmaxxing' problematic - leaderboard scores don't reflect real-world capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/state-of-llms-2025\" target=\"_blank\">Sebastian Raschka</a> | Blog\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">DeepSeek R1</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">RLVR</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">GRPO</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2025-12-25</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/year-in-review-2025/\" target=\"_blank\">2025 LLM Year in Review: RLVR and Vibe Coding Paradigm Shifts</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Karpathy's review: RLVR emerges as major training stage. Natural language becoming primary programming language - 'vibe coding'. AI writes most code for experienced developers. Rise of Cursor and Claude Code.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/year-in-review-2025/\" target=\"_blank\">Andrej Karpathy</a> | Blog\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">RLVR</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">vibe coding</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">paradigm shift</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2025-12-19</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Developer Sentiment Paradox: 90% Usage but Decreasing Positive Sentiment</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        90% of developers use AI tools regularly, but positive sentiment decreased from 70%+ in 2023-2024 to lower levels in 2025. Suggests developers are more discerning about effective AI usage patterns.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Industry Surveys</a> | Research\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">developer sentiment</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">AI adoption</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-01-15</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison: LLM Predictions for 2026 and Claude Cowork</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Willison's 2026 predictions: Fly's Sprites.dev addresses dev and API sandboxes. Porting open source with LLMs presents opportunities. Claude Cowork represents emerging general agent category.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/\" target=\"_blank\">Simon Willison</a> | Blog\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM predictions</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude Cowork</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2026-01-08</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://medium.com/@ant-oss/open-source-llm-development-2025-landscape-trends-and-insights-4e821bceba68\" target=\"_blank\">AI Coding Market Reaches $7.37B in 2025 with 85% Developer Adoption</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Market reached $7.37B in 2025, projected $23.97B by 2030. 85% of developers use AI coding tools. TypeScript surge partly due to AI assistance. Positive sentiment decreased despite high usage.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://medium.com/@ant-oss/open-source-llm-development-2025-landscape-trends-and-insights-4e821bceba68\" target=\"_blank\">Industry Analysis</a> | TechMedia\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">market analysis</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">TypeScript</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2025-05-15</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5TgLWSADJQE\" target=\"_blank\">Replit's $9B Valuation and 'Vibe Coding' Revolution</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n                        Replit reached $9B valuation serving 34M users. Amjad Masad promotes 'vibe coding' - building apps 'like doodling on a whiteboard' with AI. Complete apps in 60 seconds from a phone.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"author\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5TgLWSADJQE\" target=\"_blank\">Amjad Masad</a> | Interview\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                        <span class=\"topic\">vibe coding</span>\n                        <span class=\"topic\">Replit</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">2025-03-20</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <div class=\"stats\">3 New Products</div>\n           